 also offer an early glimpse of how AI models will contribute to scientific progress. cite11†AnnouncementsSep 10, 2026 Detecting and countering misuse of AI: September 2026 Over the past eight months, our Threat Intelligence team identified and disrupted operations in which threat actors tried to use Claude for malicious activity.\nL20: In this report, we share case studies from those operations and describe how malicious use of Claude has evolved since our previous threat reports in 2025. L21: ## News\nL22: \nL23: Search[Input: Search]\nL24: \nL25: Date Category Title\nL26:   * cite12†Sep 23, 2026Science Claude discovers a novel enzyme system with CRISPR-like repeats L27:   * cite13†Sep 18, 2026Announcements Partnering with Accenture on embedded evaluation L28:   * cite14†Sep 17, 2026Announcements Introducing the Life Sciences Verification Program L29:   * cite15†Sep 1, 2026Announcements Developing Enterprise Frontier Safeguards with our customers L30:   * cite16†Aug 31, 2026Announcements Improving our alignment and security efforts L31:   * cite17†Aug 27, 2026Announcements Previewing the Model Hardware Standard L32:   * cite18†Aug 27, 2026Announcements Expanding our support for scientists L33:   * cite19†Aug 25, 2026Announcements Funding better evaluations of AI’s impact on wellbeing L34:   * cite20†Aug 14, 2026Announcements How Claude’s text watermark works L35:   * cite21†Aug 7, 2026Product Improving Fable 5's biology safeguards L36: cite22†See more --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRelease notes  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog)\nciteturn1165view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 979\nL0: [Button: ]\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search]\nL3: \nL4: `/`\nL5: \nL6:   * English\nL7:   * Deutsch\nL8:   * Español – América Latina\nL9:   * Français\nL10:   * Indonesia\nL11:   * Italiano\nL12:   * Polski\nL13:   * Português – Brasil\nL14:   * Shqip\nL15:   * Tiếng Việt\nL16:   * Türkçe\nL17:   * Русский\nL18:   * עברית\nL19:   * العربيّة\nL20:   * فارسی\nL21:   * हिंदी\nL22:   * বাংলা\nL23:   * ภาษาไทย\nL24:   * 中文 – 简体\nL25:   * 中文 – 繁體\nL26:   * 日本語\nL27:   * 한국어\nL28: cite0†Get API key†aistudio.google.com cite1†Cookbook†github.com cite2†Community†discuss.ai.google.dev Sign in\nL29: \nL30: cite3†Docs cite4†API reference L31: \nL32: [Input: Filter]\nL33: \nL34: [Button: ]\nL35: \nL36:   * Get started\nL37: \nL38:   * Models\nL39:   * Lyria 3.5 & Lyria Clip\nL40: \nL41:   * Text-to-speech\nL42: \nL43:   * Robotics\nL44: \nL45:   * Core capabilities\nL46: \nL47:   * Image\nL48: \nL49:   * Video\nL50: \nL51:   * Speech and audio\nL52: \nL53:   * Thinking\nL54: \nL55:   * Agents\nL56: \nL57:   * Tools\nL58: \nL59:   * Live API\nL60: \nL61:   * Get started\nL62: \nL63:   * cite5†Thinking L64:   * Optimization\nL65: \nL66:   * Guides\nL67: \nL68:   * File input\nL69: \nL70:   * Logs and datasets\nL71: \nL72:   * Safety\nL73: \nL74:   * Frameworks\nL75: \nL76:   * Resources\nL77: \nL78:   * Migration\nL79: \nL80:   * cite6†Status†aistudio.google.com L81:   * Google AI Studio\nL82: \nL83:   * Google Cloud Platform\nL84: \nL85:   * Policies\nL86: \nL87: [Button: Send feedback ]\nL88: # Release notes\nL89: \nL90: This page documents updates to the Gemini API.\nL91: ## September 22, 2026\nL92: \nL93:   * Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS and Gemini 3.8 Flash-Lite TTS generally available (GA): Released our next-generation text-to-speech (TTS) audio models and the Gemini API Voices endpoint (`/v1beta/voices`):\nL94:     * cite7†Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS (`gemini-3.8-flash-tts`): Flagship creative TTS model engineered for studio-grade voice fidelity, nuanced acting, regional dialects, and long-form multi-turn stability.\nL95:     * cite8†Gemini 3.8 Flash-Lite TTS (`gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts`): Fast, cost-efficient TTS model built to replace `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview` for high-throughput production and real-time voice agent cascades.\nL96:     * cite9†Voice design , cite10†Voice replication , and the cite11†Extended Voice Library : Create persistent custom vocal personas from text prompts, replicate voices with consent verification, and query 150+ prebuilt and custom voices.\nL97: See the cite12†Text-to-speech guide to get started.\nL98: ## September 18, 2026\nL99: \nL100:   * Gemini 2.5 models access update: To ensure reliable performance for everyone, we are limiting access to the 2.5 models to users who have actively used them in the past. These models are not deprecated and will continue to be served until further notice through the API. For any new projects, use our latest models: 3.5 Flash-Lite or 3.8 Flash. This helps us maintain sufficient capacity for both ongoing legacy workflows and new applications.\nL101: ## September 17, 2026\nL102: \nL103:   * Antigravity Agent 09-2026: Released `antigravity-preview-09-2026`, which replaces and deprecates `antigravity-preview-05-2026`.\nL104: \nL105: If you run on a remote sandbox (`environment: \"remote\"`) and read only `output_text` or `model_output` steps, update the agent string and nothing else changes.\nL106: If you run tools locally (`local_environment`) or parse `function_call` steps, the built-in tools changed. Parameters use PascalCase instead of snake_case, and file edits use line-range replacements instead of full rewrites.\nL107: Capability  | 05-2026  | 09-2026\nL108: --- | --- | ---\nL109: File creation  | `write_file(path, content)`  | `write_to_file(TargetFile, CodeContent, Overwrite, Description)`\nL110: File editing  | `write_file(path, content)`, full rewrite  | `replace_file_content(TargetFile, StartLine, EndLine, TargetContent, ReplacementContent)`\nL111: File reading  | `read_file(path, offset, limit)`, byte offsets  | `view_file(AbsolutePath, StartLine, EndLine, ContentOffset)`\nL112: Directory listing  | `list_files(path)`  | `list_dir(DirectoryPath)`\nL113: File and code search  | None, agents used shell commands  | `find_by_name(SearchDirectory, Pattern, MaxDepth)` and `grep_search(SearchPath, Query, IsRegex)`\nL114: Shell execution  | `code_execution(command, timeout_seconds)`  | Unchanged\nL115: Web search  | `google_search(queries)`  | Unchanged\nL116: See the cite13†Antigravity Agent guide. `antigravity-preview-05-2026` shuts down on October 5, 2026, tracked on the cite14†deprecations page.\nL117: ## September 15, 2026\nL118: \nL119:   * Gemini 3.8 Live and Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking generally available (GA): Released two new audio-to-audio models for real-time voice applications using the Live API:\nL120:     * Gemini 3.8 Live (cite15†`gemini-3.8-live` ): The default option for most low-latency voice agent experiences and real-time dialogue without reasoning delays. Features interleaved reasoning, default asynchronous function calling, and full session client content updates.\nL121:     * Gemini 3.8 Live Extended Thinking (cite16†`gemini-3.8-live-extended-thinking` ): High-reasoning audio-to-audio model supporting background reasoning during live audio interactions, recommended when higher background reasoning is required.\nL122: To get started, see the cite17†Live API guide , the cite18†Capabilities guide , and the cite5†Thinking guide .\nL123: ## September 3, 2026\nL124: \nL125:   * Lyria 3.5 generally available (GA): Released the next generation of Google's music generation model:\nL126: \nL127:     * cite19†`lyria-3.5` : Full-length song generation with improved musical coherence, natural vocals, and fine-grained duration and structural control.\nL128: \nL129: The model supports text and image inputs and generates high-fidelity 44.1 kHz stereo audio. See the cite20†Music generation guide for details and code samples.\nL130: ## September 2, 2026\nL131: \nL132:   * Gemini 3.8 Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-3.8-flash`, our most intelligent Flash model, engineered for long-horizon software engineering, autonomous agents, and complex enterprise workflows.\nL133: \nL134: To get started, see the cite21†Gemini 3.8 Flash model page and the cite22†Latest model guide .\nL135: ## September 1, 2026\nL136: \nL137:   * Agentic video understanding: Released agentic video understanding for Gemini 3.7 Flash, 3.6 Flash, and 3.5 Flash-Lite across the Interactions and GenerateContent APIs. The model dynamically navigates video timelines, requesting transcripts, frames, or audio tracks on demand. This approach uses up to 88% fewer tokens for long-form content compared to static processing.\nL138: \nL139: To get started, see the cite23†Agentic video understanding guide.\nL140: ## August 27, 2026\nL141: \nL142:   * Gemini Omni Flash generally available (GA): Released `gemini-omni-1.1-flash`, the GA version of our fast, conversational video generation and editing model. This release includes significant new capabilities:\nL143:     * Video extension: Seamlessly extend existing videos by generating continuations at the end of a clip using the `extend` task or directly with a prompt.\nL144:     * Interpolation (first + last frame): Generate a video transitioning between two images using the `image_to_video` task with up to 2 images.\nL145:     * Resolution control: New `resolution` parameter in `video_config` supports `360p`, `720p` (default), `1080p`, and `4k` outputs. 1080p and 4K outputs are generated using upscaling.\nL146: The existing `gemini-omni-flash-preview` endpoint will be deprecated on September 30, 2026.\nL147: \nL148: To get started, see the cite24†Gemini Omni Flash model page and the cite25†omni guide .\nL149: ## August 26, 2026\nL150: \nL151:   * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe generally available (GA): Released two dedicated speech-to-text models based on Gemini's audio understanding:\nL152:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe (`gemini-3.5-transcribe`): High-accuracy, low-latency non-streaming speech-to-text with utterance-based language detection across 85+ languages, speaker diarization, word-level timestamps, and custom vocabulary biasing (up to 1,000 terms).\nL153:     * Gemini 3.5 Transcribe Live (`gemini-3.5-transcribe-live`): Low-latency, bidirectional streaming speech-to-text over WebSockets using the Live API, supporting interim and finalized transcription events, Smart transcription mode, and multiple Voice Activity Detection (VAD) strategies.\nL154: To get started, see the cite26†Audio transcription guide , the cite27†Live transcription guide , and the cite28†Gemini 3.5 Transcribe model page .\nL155: ## August 13, 2026\nL156: \nL157:   * Gemini 3.7 Flash generally available (GA): Released our most intelligent workhorse model yet for coding and agents:\nL158: \nL159:     * Gemini 3.7 Flash (`gemini-3.7-flash`): Substantial improvements across software engineering, web development, and agentic workflows, available at an introductory price through December 31, 2026.\nL160: \nL161: To get started, see the cite29†Gemini 3.7 Flash model page and the cite22†Latest model guide .\nL162: ## July 30, 2026\nL163: \nL164:   * Gemini Robotics ER 2 in public preview: Released two new embodied reasoning model endpoints for robotics:\nL165: \nL166:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-preview`: Advanced spatial reasoning, agentic code execution, multi-step tool orchestration, video moment finding, progress classification, and multi-robot coordination.\nL167:     * `gemini-robotics-er-2-streaming-preview`: Optimized for real-time text streaming using the Live API, enabling low-latency robot agents with bidirectional audio and video input.\nL168: Both model endpoints accept text, image, video, and audio inputs and support function calling with blocking behavior for physical robot actions. To get started, see the cite30†Gemini Robotics ER overview . For real-time streaming use cases, see cite31†Robotics with streaming .\nL169: \nL170:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` model will be cite32†shut down on August 31, 2026.\nL171: ## July 21, 2026\nL172: \nL173:   * Gemini 3.6 Flash and Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite generally available (GA): Released stable, production-ready versions of our latest 3.x Flash models:\nL174:     * Gemini 3.6 Flash (`gemini-3.6-flash`): Features improved token efficiency and code/agentic planning capabilities at a lower price point than 3.5 Flash, resolving developer feedback around output verbosity.\nL175:     * Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite (`gemini-3.5-flash-lite`): Offers a low-latency, highly cost-effective subagent option designed for high-volume automation.\nL176: \nL177: To learn more, see the cite22†Latest Gemini model guide.\nL178:   * Deprecated parameters: The sampling parameters `temperature`, `top_p` and `top_k` are now deprecated. See the cite33†Latest Gemini Model for details.\nL179: ## July 6, 2026\nL180: \nL181:   * cite34†Developer logs support for the Interactions API: logs for supported Interactions API calls are now viewable in the cite35†AI Studio dashboard†aistudio.google.com .\nL182: ## June 30, 2026\nL183: \nL184:   * Gemini Omni Flash in public preview: Released `gemini-omni-flash-preview`, a high-performance multimodal model designed for high-speed video generation and conversational video editing. Using the cite36†Interactions API , you can generate 3–10 second videos at 720p from text descriptions or animate still images, and then conversationally edit and refine the outputs. To get started, see the cite25†Gemini Omni Flash guide and the cite24†Gemini Omni Flash model card.\nL185:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` (Nano Banana 2 Lite) to general availability (GA), our built-in multimodal model optimized for ultra-low latency and cost-effective image generation and editing. See the cite37†Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Image model card and the cite38†Image generation guide.\nL186: ## June 24, 2026\nL187: \nL188:   * Computer Use: Launched public preview support for the cite39†Computer Use tool in Gemini 3.5 Flash. This release includes simplified actions with intents, built-in support for browser, mobile, and desktop environments, configurable safety policies, and advanced prompt injection detection.\nL189: ## June 17, 2026\nL190: \nL191:   * Streaming support for speech generation: Streaming via `streamGenerateContent` (and `stream: true` in the Interactions API) is now supported for the `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview` model. To learn more, see the cite40†Text-to-Speech guide.\nL192: ## June 15, 2026\nL193: \nL194:   * Deprecation announcement: The following image generation models are being deprecated and will be cite32†shut down on August 17, 2026:\nL195: \nL196:     * Imagen 4 and Gemini 3 Image models:\nL197:       * `imagen-4.0-generate-001`\nL198:       * `imagen-4.0-ultra-generate-001`\nL199:       * `imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001`\nL200: \nL201: To migrate your code to newer stable or preview endpoints, refer to the cite41†Gemini deprecations page.\nL202:   * Deprecation announcement: The following video generation models are being deprecated and will be cite32†shut down on June 30, 2026:\nL203: \nL204:     * Veo models:\nL205:       * `veo-2.0-generate-001`\nL206:       * `veo-3.0-generate-001`\nL207:       * `veo-3.0-fast-generate-001`\nL208: Update your integration to either use the Veo 3.1 preview model IDs (`veo-3.1-generate-preview`, `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`) or the 3.1 GA models available through the cite42†Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform†docs.cloud.google.com to avoid service interruptions.\nL209: \nL210:   * Deprecation announcement: The experimental GMP Contextual View tool (a fixed interface for Grounding with Google Maps outputs) will cite32†shut down on June 15, 2026:\nL211: ## June 1, 2026\nL212: \nL213:   * The following Gemini 2.0 models are now cite32†shut down :\nL214: \nL215:     * `gemini-2.0-flash`\nL216:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-001`\nL217:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite`\nL218:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001`\nL219: \nL220: Use cite43†`gemini-3.5-flash` or cite44†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL221: ## May 28, 2026\nL222: \nL223:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-image` (Nano Banana 2) and `gemini-3-pro-image` (Nano Banana Pro), the generally available (GA) versions of our native visual models, cite45†Gemini 3.1 Flash Image and cite46†Gemini 3 Pro Image .\nL224:   * Video-to-image generation support: You can now pass a video file (via direct upload or as a public YouTube URL) as multimodal context alongside a text prompt to generate high-quality thumbnails, cinematic movie posters, or summary infographics. This feature is supported exclusively on the `gemini-3.1-flash-image` model. To learn more, see the cite47†Video-to-image generation guide.\nL225:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` models are deprecated and will be cite32†shut down on June 25, 2026.\nL226: ## May 25, 2026\nL227: \nL228:   * The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model has been cite32†shut down . Use cite44†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL229: ## May 19, 2026\nL230: \nL231:   * Released `gemini-3.5-flash`, the generally available (GA) version of cite43†Gemini 3.5 Flash , our most intelligent model for sustained frontier performance on agentic and coding tasks. This is now the model behind `gemini-flash-latest`.\nL232:   * Launched the Managed Agents in the Gemini API in public preview. This enables developers to build and deploy autonomous, stateful agents that run in secure, isolated Google-hosted Linux sandbox environments. To learn more, see the cite48†Agents overview page and the cite49†Quickstart .\nL233:   * Released the general-purpose Antigravity Agent managed agent, cite50†`antigravity-preview-05-2026` , in public preview. The Antigravity agent can autonomously plan, reason, write and execute code, manage files, and browse the web inside its sandbox container. See the cite13†Antigravity Agent guide for code samples and specifications.\nL234: ## May 7, 2026\nL235: \nL236:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, the generally available (GA) version of cite44†Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite , optimized for speed, scale, and cost efficiency.\nL237: \nL238:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model is deprecating on 5/11/26 and will be cite32†shut down on May 25, 2026.\nL239: ## May 6, 2026\nL240: \nL241:   * Upcoming breaking change: The cite36†Interactions API request and response schema (`outputs` → `steps`) and output format configuration (`response_format`) are changing. The new schema becomes the default on May 26 and the legacy schema will be removed on June 8. See the cite51†migration guide for details.\nL242: ## May 5, 2026\nL243: \nL244:   * Updated File Search to support multimodal search. You can now natively embed and search through images using the `gemini-embedding-2` model. Grounding metadata now includes `media_id` for visual citations and `page_numbers` that indicate where information is found. To learn more, see the cite52†File Search guide.\nL245: \nL246: ## May 4, 2026\nL247: \nL248:   * Launched event-driven cite53†Webhooks support in the Gemini API to replace polling workflows for the Batch API and long-running operations.\nL249: ## April 30, 2026\nL250: \nL251:   * The `gemini-robotics-er-1.5-preview` model has been cite32†shut down . Use cite54†`gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` instead.\nL252: \nL253: ## April 22, 2026\nL254: \nL255:   * Released `gemini-embedding-2` as generally available (GA). To learn more, see the cite55†Embeddings page.\nL256: ## April 21, 2026\nL257: \nL258:   * Released new versions of the cite56†Deep Research agent with collaborative planning, visualization support, MCP server integration, and File Search:\nL259: \nL260:     * cite57†`deep-research-preview-04-2026` : Designed for speed and efficiency, ideal to be streamed back to a client UI.\nL261:     * cite58†`deep-research-max-preview-04-2026` : Maximum comprehensiveness for automated context gathering and synthesis.\nL262: ## April 15, 2026\nL263: \nL264:   * Launched cite59†Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS Preview , our cost-efficient, expressive, and steerable text to speech model. Read the cite12†Text-to-Speech docs to learn more.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nArtificial intelligence | AP News (https://apnews.com/hub/artificial-intelligence)\nciteturn1165view3 [wordlim: 100] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://apnews.com/hub/artificial-intelligence\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 2025\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMachine learning - Latest research and news | Nature (https://www.nature.com/subjects/machine-learning)\nciteturn1165view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.nature.com/subjects/machine-learning\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 248\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPress Releases | Federal Trade Commission (https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases)\nciteturn1165view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 190\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOur Work | Electronic Frontier Foundation (https://www.eff.org/updates)\nciteturn1165view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.eff.org/updates\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 268\n-------------------------------------------------